From 267973a4c5017aa843dbb1ea2bb162cf1fc4324c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:12:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 096/294] pco: lower loops that every instance runs alike to
 plain branches

A loop whose breaks and continues all sit under uniform conditions runs
the same iterations in every instance, so it needs none of the execution
mask counting (cndst, cndsm, cndend, cndlt) of the general lowering.

Uniformity now follows virtual registers through their writers, with a
writer that reads the register again (a loop counter) accepted, and
requires every writer to sit where all instances execute. A pre-pass
decides which ifs and loops are uniform; the lowering pass then keeps
the masking nesting count as before. A uniform loop's break branches to
an exit block after the back edge, a continue branches to the back
edge, both on the same condition as the break or continue.

The condition producers are no longer made (ignorepe): every instance
is active wherever a uniform if or loop is lowered, and a producer
inside a divergent loop would keep running for instances that already
left it.

The register allocator takes the start of a loop from its body when the
prologue block is empty, and extends the life of a value whose last use
is the loop's first instruction.

glmark2 loop fragment-uniform=true (zink, off-screen): the loop body goes
from 11 to 9 instruction groups per iteration with no control ops, 397 ->
502 FPS. Other scenes unchanged. CTS unchanged: glsl loops, switch,
functions, return, discard, demote, subgroups vote/ballot/basic, SPIR-V
control flow, graphicsfuzz, and the pco, caselist, compute, robustness,
UBO, null image, TFBC and dynamic rendering lists.
