+/* Uniformity: a value is the same in every instance when it is computed only
+ * by pure ALU ops from shared registers, constants and immediates. A virtual
+ * register is uniform when all its writers are, and every instance executes
+ * them; a writer that reads the register again (a loop counter) is fine.
